messages.content:
give me visual artifacts

IMPORTANT: You MUST respond with actual chart data in JSON format wrapped in ```json code fences. Use one of these chart types: bar, line, pie, table, process, timeline. Format example for bar chart: ```json
{"type":"bar","title":"Chart Title","labels":["A","B","C"],"values":[10,20,30]}
``` For comparison/table: ```json
{"type":"table","title":"Comparison","headers":["Attribute","Edge","Cloud"],"rows":[["Latency","1-10ms","50-250ms"],["Privacy","High","Moderate"]]}
``` For process/flow: ```json
{"type":"process","title":"Flow","steps":["Step 1","Step 2","Step 3"]}
``` For pie: ```json
{"type":"pie","title":"Distribution","labels":["A","B"],"values":[60,40]}
``` For timeline: ```json
{"type":"timeline","title":"Timeline","events":[{"date":"Phase 1","description":"Description"}]}
``` You can include MULTIPLE ```json blocks if the user asks for multiple charts. Include a brief text explanation before each chart. DO NOT just describe charts in text — you MUST include the JSON data so the charts render visually.
